# Build context exclusions for reg_webapp/Dockerfile (context = repo root).
# Keep the context lean + deterministic, and DEFEND #224 provenance confinement
# at the context boundary (assertion #3, alongside the in-image RUN check):
# a maintainer's local build-db writes reg_meta.provenance.db* next to the
# catalog DB, and any reg_meta.db / *.db lying around the working tree must never
# enter the image — `reg-meta update` re-fetches the release DB at build time.

# --- #224: maintainer-only provenance debug sibling (never ships) ---
**/reg_meta.provenance.db
**/reg_meta.provenance.db-*
**/reg_meta.provenance.db*

# --- Local DB artifacts (the image bakes its own via `reg-meta update`) ---
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db.zst
**/*.zst

# --- Real SCB/SOS seed + build inputs (untracked, large, never in the image) ---
reg_meta_build/input_data/

# --- VCS / agent / editor cruft ---
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.agents/
.venv/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/.DS_Store

# --- Node / bun build state (bun reinstalls from the lockfile in-image) ---
**/node_modules/
reg_webapp/frontend/dist/

# --- Docs / specs not needed to build or run ---
# NOTE: do NOT blanket-exclude **/*.md — several member pyprojects set
# `readme = "README.md"`, so hatchling's editable build reads them in-image.
archive/
REFACTOR_SPEC.md
ARCHITECTURE.md
AGENTS.md

# >>> yard init: Docker build context >>>
# Yard builds every lane worker and gate image from this directory as the
# Docker build context, so whatever is not excluded here is copied to the
# daemon on each build. Yard owns the two entries below; the rest of the file
# is yours, and this block is appended once and never rewritten.
#
# .yard/local is Yard's own local state — the store, logs, lane workspaces, and
# a live daemon socket, which is not a file a build context can carry at all.
# .git is large, and it is also the main source of image-digest divergence
# between gates: each gate builds from a fresh detached view whose .git differs,
# so a COPY that reaches it misses the layer cache every time.
.git
.yard/local
#
# Your build output belongs here too. Yard does not know which trees this
# project has, so these are suggestions — uncomment what applies, delete the
# rest, and add your own:
# target/
# node_modules/
# dist/
# <<< yard init: Docker build context <<<
